================================================================================
Data
================================================================================

Restriction-enzyme recognition sequences appearing in
prototype/dna-reader.html and reference/python/tests/validate_digest.py were
transcribed independently from standard published references. They are
statements of biological fact about approximately fifty well-known Type II
enzymes, not a reproduction of any database.

Production enzyme data will be sourced from REBASE (Roberts lab, New England
Biolabs) and packaged in a SEPARATE repository under REBASE's own terms with
its own NOTICE. REBASE data is not Apache-2.0 and must not be commingled with
this repository's code.

  REBASE                http://rebase.neb.com/
  Citation              Roberts RJ, Vincze T, Posfai J, Macelis D.
                        REBASE: a database for DNA restriction and modification.
                        Nucleic Acids Research.

The planned annotation database (polylinker-features) will be CC BY 4.0 and
will live in a separate repository, sourced from UniProt/Swiss-Prot, Rfam,
FPbase and NCBI UniVec, with per-entry attribution.

The planned correctness benchmark (polylinker-bench) will be CC0.

